# flabel's `reference.config` — deliberately empty of mappings.
#
# It exists so that Suricata does NOT fall back to `/etc/suricata/reference.config`, which is a
# package-managed file on whatever machine happens to run the labelling. `config_sha256` covers
# this file; it cannot cover one that varies per box.
#
# Empty is the right content, not a placeholder. This file maps a `reference:` keyword's prefix to
# a URL, nothing in flabel reads those URLs, and measured against a real 85,545-rule snapshot its
# absence changes the load by 0 rules — the engine warns once per unknown prefix and carries on.
# The point is to own the path, not to populate it.
